  "note": "The single source for the three design directions. `npm run check:contrast` verifies every pair below against WCAG 2.1 AA; step 10 turns the chosen direction into CSS custom properties from this same file. Two border tokens on purpose: `border` separates a card from the page and is decorative, which WCAG 1.4.11 does not govern — forcing 3:1 on every card edge is why some 'accessible' interfaces look like spreadsheets. `borderStrong` is for boundaries a person must perceive to use a control (inputs, checkboxes, segmented controls) and is held to 3:1.",
